    {
      "kind": "wiki",
      "evidence": "data/content/dungeons/darvon_s_descent.json: difficulty 4, zone 'Sanctuary (Memorial Caverns)', enemies ['Darvon', 'Changelings', 'Changeling Bruisers', 'Changeling Arcanus', 'Bats', 'Changeling Bruiser', 'Changeling Arcanus', 'Darvon']."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reference",
      "evidence": "Door at [-903.48, -47.87, 239.34]: BJX fork Battles.lua:32 (Npcs.json Id 46211, sh_cave_entrance_bat_cave_01.adr). (R) the fork's own placement, not a captured one. Region Sanctuary, place Sanctuary."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reference",
      "evidence": "BJX fork Resources/Battles.json Id 14 ('Darvon's Descent (the live dungeon: Darvon's changelings across the root caverns, Darvon at the wing shrine at'): scene sg_changeling_caverns, entry, exit, 8 waves, 31 spawns ({'Changeling Defiler': 11, 'Changeling Bruiser': 10, 'Changeling Thief': 9, 'Darvon': 1})."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Every spot inside the scene is the fork's generated layout, not an original one. Zone number 1213 is the fork's; ours must be assigned and the scene sg_changeling_caverns has not been loaded by our server yet (the eleven shipped battles all use sg_random_encounter_clearing). Triggers: at-start spawns are actors, later waves follow the one before (the fork's 1.5 s delay is dropped). Knockouts and score are the design's defaults; coins and XP are the shipped battles' values, not the fork's 60 coins / 220 stars."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Not proven in the client: this scene needs one native load, and the starter or door of `entry` is drawn by the entrances work, not by this file. Each kind's rank here decides its health and hit at the fight's tier. Door actor 100000046211: reference Npcs.json Id 46211, model 251, name 7697, at [-903.48, -47.87, 239.34]."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) The guide's main goal is the one goal shown from the start and is done with the fork's last goal; the steps before it stay, as the triggers of its waves and boss."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Guide overlay by scripts/dungeon_fights.py from data/content/dungeons/darvon_s_descent.json."
    },
    {
      "kind": "wiki",
      "evidence": "rc-0137 prize wheel: fandom 'Darvon's Descent' (revision 49144) lists one prize wheel per combat job and a 132-coin slot; any other job spins the items every job's wheel holds. Ninja: the wiki's 'Ninja's Neckace of Vitality IV' is 'Ninja's Necklace of Vitality IV' in our record dungeons/darvon_s_descent.json."
    }
  ]
